            "review_title": "Review at Little Hanoi Restaurants",
            "review_text": "Ron Y\n5 contributions\n0\nGreat little restaurant for a great dinner\nMay 2026 • Couples\nMy wife and I and another couple arrived in the Old Quarter in Hanoi the previous day having had dinner at the hotel restaurant, OK.\nWe decided to find an alternative place to eat.We ventured around the area and noticed the Little Hanoi restaurant,looked at the menu and their advertising “Home style cooking”.\nWe booked for that evening and glad we did ,the food was great the staff were extremely welcoming and efficient.\nWe shared five main dishes and with steamed rice together with beers the cost was a shock, just over one million Dong.\nWe equated to $25 Aussie per couple.\nIt is not the just the cost all the meals were great ,we agreed to have the stir fried egg plant recommend by the manager,it was top shelf.\nLittle Hanoi restaurant had a nice vibe and it was only a stone’s throw from the Tirant hotel where were were staying.\nWe enjoyed the meal that much we went back a second time.\nRead more\nWritten May 31, 2026",
