            "review_text": "Andrew D\nEdinburgh, United Kingdom37 contributions\n0\nA lively, tasty, eating out experience in the old town.\nNov 2025 • Couples\nWe chose this restaurant simply because it was next to our hotel. We had tried a couple of others a bit of a walk away on previous evenings, but should simply have come here each night. The atmosphere is lively with the proprietor acting as main host and master of ceremonies. The menu is varied with lots of things we recognised. The food itself was wonderful. Delivered quickly, big portions, and very tasty. The drinks are cheap and theist gave each of us a shot of local hooch to round the evening out. Two starters, two mains, two drinks each, and change out of £15. What's not to like. Overall a real find.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nA great place for a good dinner. Portions are quite large. Remarkable value by UK standards. Just enjoy.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 10, 2025",
