            "review_text": "Axel K\nNelson, New Zealand57 contributions\n1\nGreat authentic food on the fringe of the Old Quarter\nAug 2025 • Solo\nA very authentic and family run restaurant. The location on the fringe of the Old Quarter makes for a nice and relaxing experience, away from busy lanes.\nThe interior has a lot of colonial ambience.\nAnd I haven't even mentioned the food yet.\nIt is absolutely delicious with a great range of traditional Vietnamese meals.\nBesides the good range of beers, bottled and draught, they serve their own rice wines, infused with a variety of fruit and even mushrooms.\nIt is one of these places I like to find on my travels, and I am becoming a regular.\nPrices are very moderate and fair.\nTry it out - you won't be disappointed.\nRead more\nWritten August 14, 2025",
